{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4efa258c-2f5f-437e-a131-233c590433b0",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Inventory Adjustment)",
    "description": "Inventory module \u2014 Inventory Adjustment (`/api/v1/inventory/adjustments`). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory (create-inventory-adjustment.dto.ts, update-inventory-adjustment.dto.ts, inventory-adjustment.response.dto.ts).\n\nMANUAL FIXTURE GAP \u2014 read before running (applies to every request in this collection): `productId` is the Business layer's own contract for Inventory Adjustment (a real, in-module numeric bigint FK, not a `productUuid` resolved to one) \u2014 there is NO endpoint anywhere that returns a Product's internal numeric id (06_DATABASE_STANDARDS.md PK-003 forbids ever serializing it \u2014 `GET /products/:uuid` only ever returns `uuid`). `{{productId}}` defaults to \"1\", a plausible first-row id on a freshly-seeded local dev DB \u2014 before running this collection, manually verify it against your local MySQL (e.g. `SELECT id FROM products WHERE uuid = '<real product uuid>'`) and replace {{productId}} with the real value. A stale/wrong {{productId}} makes every request fail with a NotFound-style domain error \u2014 a sign of a stale fixture, not proof this collection is broken. `{{warehouseUuid}}` similarly defaults to \"\" and must be filled in from a real Warehouse (create one via the sibling `Warehouse.postman_collection.json`) before running this collection. Same treatment the repo already gives other manual-fixture gaps (Authentication hardcodes `tenantId=1`; Warehouse needs a manual `branchUuid`).\n\nEvery route requires `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` AND `X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}`. No Authorization header at all fails jwt-auth.middleware.ts before this module's own request validation ever runs \u2014 401 `AUTH_MISSING_TOKEN`. A missing/malformed `X-Tenant-Id` header, or a malformed request body, is rejected as 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Business errors not individually mapped fall back to 422 `INV_DOMAIN_ERROR` (domain-error-http-mapping.ts).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
